From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:34:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] engine: allocate on the caller's FNA relay for inbound calls

Backport of upstream 8e4008f ("fix(engine): allocate on the caller's
FNA relay for inbound calls (#9)"):

  An inbound call's uplink RTP lands on the relay the caller marked
  is_fna=1 in the offer. getMediaRelayEndpoint always picked a non-FNA
  endpoint, so for inbound calls we allocated on a relay the peer never
  feeds: the call connects but no inbound RTP is ever bridged and the
  callee hears nothing.

  Prefer the is_fna=1 endpoint when the call is inbound, threading an
  `inbound` flag from maybeStartMedia (m.direction ==
  CallDirectionIncoming) through runMedia and connectAndAllocate into
  getMediaRelayEndpoint. Outbound behaviour is unchanged.

Adapted to this tree: connectAndAllocate keeps the peerSubscriptions
argument the video media path patch added, and the relay diagnostics
in onRelay pick the endpoint the same way the media path does.

The "connecting media transport to relay" log line now also says
whether the endpoint is FNA, whether the call is inbound and how many
endpoints the relay offered, so a device log shows the choice without
the diagnostics recorder.

relay_endpoint_test.go pins the choice, including an offer shaped like
the one an Android caller sent on 30 October 2026, which marks no
relay is_fna: for that offer the choice does not change. The two
newMediaSrtcpSender calls in engine_media_test.go get the RTCP CNAME
argument the video media path patch added, so the package's tests
compile again.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/purpshell/meowcaller/commit/8e4008f12884cf15dc487f1d4afc83055275f966]
